---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import config from '../../site.config.json';
import { stats } from '../lib/data.js';
---
<Base title={`${config.SITE_NAME} API — free government processing-time data`}
      description="Free, no-key JSON API for official government processing times, latest route values and history, plus an MCP server for AI agents.">
  <h1>JSON API (static, free, no key)</h1>
  <p>The entire dataset is prebuilt as static JSON — fast, cacheable, and stable. Attribution (CC BY 4.0) required. Full schema: <a href="/api/v1/openapi.yaml">OpenAPI 3.1 spec</a>.</p>

  <h2>Endpoints</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/index.json</code></td><td>Dataset stats, sources, and links to all collections</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/jurisdictions/ca.json</code></td><td>All Canadian routes with latest values</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/jurisdictions/gb.json</code></td><td>All UK routes with latest values</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/jurisdictions/nz.json</code></td><td>All New Zealand visa types with 50% and 80% working-day metrics</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/jurisdictions/no.json</code></td><td>All table-backed Norway UDI waiting-time routes with official update dates</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/ircc-forward-looking.json</code></td><td>All IRCC forward-looking programs, current queue estimates and application-month cohorts</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/services/&#123;service_key&#125;.json</code></td><td>One service, all applicant countries (e.g. <code>ca-visitor-visa</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>/api/v1/entities/&#123;entity_id&#125;.json</code></td><td>One route: latest value + full recorded history (e.g. <code>ca-visitor-visa--in</code>)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <pre class="fresh" style="overflow-x:auto"><code>curl {config.SITE_URL}/api/v1/entities/ca-visitor-visa--in.json</code></pre>
  <p class="small muted">For New Zealand, each visa service has separate <code>--p50</code> and <code>--p80</code> entities. The numeric value remains a working-day count and is labeled <code>unit_original: "working days"</code>.</p>
  <p class="small muted">For a published range such as UDI’s <code>15–29 days</code>, <code>value_raw</code> keeps the full official range and <code>value_days</code> uses its upper end for conservative comparison.</p>
  <p class="small muted">IRCC forward-looking records use <code>metric_type: "forward"</code>. Their <code>cohort_month</code> is when an application was submitted within a current IRCC snapshot—not the date IRCC published that value. Snapshot dates remain separate so the two timelines cannot be silently mixed.</p>

  <h2>For AI agents</h2>
  <p>An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server exposes <code>search_entities</code>, <code>get_entity</code>, <code>get_latest_value</code> and <code>compare_values</code> over this dataset — see the <a href="https://github.com/artwisdom/govwait/tree/main/machine/mcp-server" rel="noopener">public MCP server repository</a> for registration instructions, and <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> for a machine-readable site description.</p>

  <p class="small muted">{stats.entities.toLocaleString()} routes · {stats.forward_looking_estimates.toLocaleString()} forward-looking headline/cohort estimates · regenerated on every data refresh · values are official government publications, republished with provenance.</p>
</Base>
